+    {"id":"beat-01-reframe","text":"When people hear the word \"entrepreneur,\" they often imagine someone launching a startup, raising money, or making a huge leap into the unknown. But for most people, entrepreneurship begins much smaller than that."},
+    {"id":"beat-02-experiments","text":"It might begin as a side project, a freelance client, a workshop you offer, a digital product you test, or a service you share with people you already know. In other words, entrepreneurship often begins as a series of experiments."},
+    {"id":"beat-03-ai-and-human","text":"In an AI-accelerated world, this kind of experimentation is even more accessible. AI tools can help you brainstorm ideas, draft offers, organize research, refine marketing language, and streamline repetitive work. But AI doesn't replace the human elements that make solo work successful: judgment, trust, relationships, and the ability to solve real problems for real people."},
